E
book quest guide~
                  &+WBASIC GUIDELINES FOR QUEST IMMORTALS ON DURIS&N

&+Y1)&n The quest immortals may not participate in any way with quests that they
   are running.   Either you run a quest, or participate; not both.

&+Y2)&n The quest immortals should wait at least one (1) hour after logging off
   their immortal before logging on any mortal character.  This obviously
   also implies that the quest immortals won't have any mortal characters
   logged on at the same time as their immortal.

&+Y3)&n While good race only and evil race only quests are okay, they should be
   evenly distributed.  For example, don't run 5 goodie quests and only 1
   evil only quest.

&+Y4)&n While answering petitions (responsibly) is fine, the quest immortals should
   not resurrect them, retrieve their corpses, etc.  The one exception to this
   is that they can resurrect or move corpses as part of their own quests.

&+Y5)&n Resurrections and corpse retrieving as mentioned above should be kept to
   a minimum.

&+Y6)&n Unique artifacts, Iouns, Full Artifacts, and level potions should never be
   given as quest rewards without explicit approval of a Forger or Overlord.

&+Y7)&n Items created as quest rewards should never be better then artifacts.

&+Y8)&n Items loaded or created as quest rewards should, for the most part, be
   similar to items in zones of similar difficulty as the quest (though
   strung to appear unique.)

&+Y9)&n If a quest immortal wants to create an item that doesn't exist in the game
   (which would therefore require special bits to be set), they need to talk
   to a Forger or Overlord first.

&+Y10)&n Quest immortals who have been granted the setbit command will NEVER use
    the command to set players under ANY CIRCUMSTANCES.

&+Y11)&n Items created for quest rewards must be earned, and never given freely.
    This includes, but is not limited to, transferring created equipment
    to your own mortal characters (either directly, or indirectly.)

&+Y12)&n These rules are completely subject to the interpretation and whims of the
    Forgers and Overlords.  In addition, the Forgers and Overlords may create
    additional rules and guidelines as they desire.
~
