E
book council~
&+WThis book details the rules and responsibilities of those elected to
&+Wrepresent the Duris playerbase on the Player Council.

&+WMeetings will be Once a week for the Council members to discuss issues,
&+Wand Once a month with the council gods to present those issues.


&+WLook page1, page2, page3, page4, page5, page6
&+Wto find out what's inside.
~
E
page1~
&+W  1.  At all times, the player rep must remember that they are there to
&+Wrepresent all players, not just themselves, their guild or their clique.
&+WThis means that You must be impartial in listening to complaints and
&+Wsuggestions, and as well, do your best to filter out the realistic ideas
&+Wand complaints from the idiotic ones.  It is suggested you take notes
&+Wbetween meetings, try to stay brief and to the point, and try to avoid
&+Wany sort of partisanship when discussing these proposed changes, but
&+Winstead, try to think of what is best for the mud as a whole.
~
E
page2~
&+W  2.  During meetings, representatives will be restricted to discussing
&+WONLY issues of the mud.  Please refrain from bitching about each other,
&+Wthe other side of the race war, or any other personal issues.  Stick to
&+Wissues which affect the MUD balance, MUD fun, etc.
~
E
page3~
&+W  3.  The term of a rep will be for three r/l months.  At the end of the
&+Wthree months, we will hold new elections, and currently there are no
&+Wterm limits.
~
E
page4~
&+W  4.  Any representative who fails to make 2 meetings in a row will be
&+Wreplaced by the person who came in 4th place after them.  Any represen-
&+Wtative who misses 4 meetings (in a row or not) will also be replaced by
&+Wthe next in line.
~
E
page5~
&+W  5.  Cython and Tripod will retain full VETO power, yet will rely as well
&+Won the reps to maintain integrity and they will only use this power for
&+Wany truly stupid issues.
~
E
page6~
&+W   6.  The council gods (Jera, Dakta and Clavados) will be responsible for
&+Wmaintaining order for the regular meetings, and as well for passing on the
&+Wfinal decisions of the Council to the Immortals after the Monthly meeting.
&+WIn case of any ties in decision-making, they will be responsible for any
&+Wtie-breaking decisions.
~
E
page7~
&+W   7.  Using your avatar to scout the opposite side of racewars of your primary character, or
&+Wusing it to pass information to the other side of racewars will result in termination of your
&+Wavatar and possibly your primary character.
~
