page1 1~
&+gGENERAL INFORMATION&N
&+g------------------&N
Gnomes are smaller cousins of the dwarfs who tend to be friendly and
heavily inclined towards magic. They generally live in hilly, wooded
regions which can offer underground homes, places where they may remain
unseen in order to pursue their joys of mining and craft undisturbed.
Gnomish society is very well organized and patterned after a clannish
system. Although gnomes are cousins of dwarves, they celebrate their hard
work with many more festivals and holidays, priding themselves on hard
work and joyous play. Gnomish people are also very inclined towards music
and the crafting of musical instruments, as well as woodcarving and
brewing.
~
E
page2 2~
&+gRACIAL APPEARANCE&N
&+g-----------------&N
The following information is provided primarily for purposes of setting
chracter descriptions or for those interested in roleplaying.

Gnomes are a long lived race which can live to be 400 to 600 years old,
not even reaching adulthood until nearly 60 years of age. They are a small
race as well, with average height being just over three feet and the
average weight being around 80 pounds. Gnomish beings have dark tan or
woody brown colored skin which is reminescient of carved wood, and of
course their most striking feature is their uncommonly large noses, fully
twice the size of the average human or dwarf. Gnomes are highly
intelligent, hence their sucess with magic, however their joyous nature
makes them less wise in the ways of the world. They sport excellent manual
dexterity which assists them in their well respected wood carving and gem
cutting endevours.
~
E
