page1 1~
&+yGENERAL INFORMATION&N
&+y-------------------&N
Ogres are considered an extension of the goblinoid races by many learned sages,
distant cousins to such vermin as kobolds, orcs, goblins, hobgoblins, bugbears
and trolls. They are commonly members of wandering scavenger bands, making a
living by abmushing, raiding and thievery. Ogre personalities tend to be
extremely violent, covetous and destructive. Seldom can one trust the nature
of an ogre, for they tend to argue over treasure, eat everything in sight, and
be generally disruptive to any group they join. Due to their ravenous natures,
ogres rarely are proficient in any trades or labors, preferring to steal what
they cannot make themselves.

Ogres are often found in the cave regions of the Faang Mountains on the island
of Azursel.
~
E
page2 2~
&+yRACIAL APPEARANCE&N
&+y-----------------&N
Most wandering ogres reach their teens before beginning their traditional roles
as bandits and maurauders and can live to be over 100 years old. Ogres tend to
be very large, dirty and brutish in appearance with hide colored a dirty yellow
and covered with darker bumps. Their teeth and nails can be orange or black and
are generally poorly kept. Ogre eyes are commonly dark purple with white pupils
and their hair is blackish-blue to dark green and usually greasy. Average
heights for ogres are 9'0" (males) and 8'10" (females) and average weights are
350 lbs (males) and 310 lbs (females).
~
