E
book ansi color~

There are 3 types of ANSI color control sequences:

&+<color> -  set foreground color.  If the color letter is uppercase, the color
             is bold.
&-<color> -  set background color.  If the color letter is uppercase, the text
             will blink.
&=<bg><fg> - set both background <bg> and foreground <fg> color, exactly the
             same restrictions as for setting foreground and background
             separately.

w - white    l - black    r - red    b - blue    g - green
y - yellow   c - cyan     m - magenta
(+w is normal text, +W is bold text)
~
