rather than for true dinner eating.  All along the edges of the rather
large, oval table are a series of intricate inlays done with various
different woods.  Inlays range in color from deep red to a pale gold, and
all are perfectly done.  This table alone is worth a vast fortune.  Its
size, and the number of tiny, intricate inlays and carvings, suggests that
it took many months to create.
