journal book~
The first two pages of this journal have been written in, and can be read by
looking at 'page1' or 'page2'. The rest, however, is still blank, and seems
to be made of very fine vellum indeed.
~
E
page1~
&+c"&+wTwo strangers came to the camp today. I don't like their complexion or their
temperament, and I harbor suspicions that they carry a little Orcish blood
in their veins. They approached Septimus and offered their services as
craftsmen; the runty one, it seems, is a woodworker, and the lanky one does
*something* with iron, I don't know what. Being the cautious, prudent man
that he is, Septimus immediately accepted, and ordered us to empty two of
the wagons for their use! I don't like this one bit, but I can't for the
life of me imagine what to do about it.&+c"

                                                &+BRellius
~
E
page2~
&+c"&+wMy fears have been realized. Today Septimus announced that we would be
halting our travels indefinitely, so as to allow the newcomers a better
working environment. What have they done, to cause our leader to blaspheme
Winduin in this manner? A pall has fallen over the entire camp; it is as
though the will of my people is being drained, overshadowed by these new
presences. I no longer even feel safe writing in this journal, and keep it
hidden deep in one of the storage wagons. I shall update the journal soon,
but for now, I go to confront this so-called 'ironworker' and find out what
it is he's really up to.&+c"

                                        &+BRellius
~
A
