paper piece tatturd sheet~
&+L   This piece of paper has notes on it describing the history and phenomena of
&+Lwhat is going on to the north.  The paper is mixed with common, magical
&+Lsymbols that are incomprehensible, and some sort of language that is
&+Lcompletely baffling.  You can make out the following passages:

&+L"&+w... that the creature has become even sicker these last few weeks.  Jhary
&+whas tried to <*+*>, but it has come to nothing. ~%_ hasn't responded to
&+wany questions, and we think that he is going /-\|...&+L"

&+L"&+w...~%_ has attacked another caravan.  We have tried to warn others, but
&+wthey need our i_i_i, so keep coming to thier deaths...&+L"

&+L"&+w...troubles are over, he's destroyed the bridge...&+L"

&+L"&+w... keep occuring. Our hunters have had a hard time bringing back game that
&+wis healthy.  Vost claims that the attacks seem to be directed now, unlike
&+wbefore. ~%_ might be the cause, but Vost thinks differently from a glimpse
&+wof a strange creature that scurried away.  We have no choice but to kill
&+wthose infected, for there seems to be no cure...&+L"

&+L"&+w... to stay away from the *|*. Eieslinn has continued to cultivate it, and
&+wit seems to keep them away...&+L"

&+L"&+w... lightnings have started.  They seem to be both the cause and effect of
&+wthe strange contagion, although small burns to heal.  All hunting parties
&+whave stopped by order of Estidan, and the stores begin to run low.  The *#*#*
&+ware calling it the &+r'&+Rburning&+r'&+w, to reflect the feeling one gets from...&+L"

&+Land a last note along the bottom the page:

&+L"&+w... tried to escape through the portal today. I told him that the other side
&+wwas unstable, but he didn't listen.  Unfortunately, he tried to take several
&+wof the *#*#* with him.  With the destruction of the portal, we have nothing
&+wleft to do but hope...&+L"&n
~
