statue~
&n   This statue of a &+gforest T&+ro&+gr&n sits here before the stone dais in
the ruined temples courtyard.  Based on the quality of craftsmanship, it must
have been an object of &+Wworship&n and &+Wreverence&n.  Something about the
&+gT&+ro&+gr&n gives it a look of majestic sadness, as well as a hidden wisdom
and intelligence.  At the base of the statue is a small carving which depicts
an epic looking battle in the giant forest, with the &+gT&+ro&+gr&n aiding the
forces of &+Wgood&n against the forces of &+Levil&n.
~
