E
flower ethereal rose~
&+gThis&n &+rflower&n &+gis a delicate object of infinite beauty, a magical creation
&+gthat rivals and perhaps surpasses any&n &+rrose&n &+gof natural origins. Crafted
&+gfrom the &+cc&+Ch&+ca&+bo&+Cs&n &+gof the &+CDre&+cam Wo&+Crld&n &+gby an insane&n &+mdrow&n &+garchmage, the spell
&+grequired to fashion the&n &+rrose&n &+gkilled the crazed &+mdrow&+g. The powers of the
&+gobject are unknown, but when held by any person, a clear voice can be
&+gheard in their head, repeating the same message endlessly, a message from
&+gthe mage to a&n &+mdrow muse&+g:&n

&+mMy dearest muse,

&+mI've told you before what you mean to me.  You've become a dear, dear
&+mfriend to me in a short period of time.  I care for you a great deal, and
&+mhope you feel the same.  Life in Aracdrathos and the Underdark can be
&+mharsh, and it amazes me that a creature of your beauty could have been
&+mspawned in such an environment.  My life, dedicated to the magical arts,
&+mhas offered me little time for companionship.  You have intrigued and
&+mcharmed me, beguiling me with your warmth and spirit, amazing me with your
&+mstrength of character and range of talents.  You have enriched an old
&+mmage's life, and could give me no greater gift than your friendship.

&+mYou may call on me at any time and know that I will be there for you,
&+moffering any and all assistance I can.  Know that you are in my thoughts
&+mand heart always.

&+gNeither the name of the mage or the drow woman that fascinated him is ever
&+gstated, and they have been forgotten over time.  All that remains of the
&+gfeelings the mage had for the muse is this timeless flower, an oddly
&+gromantic gesture from a race known mostly for cruelty and hate.
~
A
