E
book remains~
This book has been fairly well preserved, due to the dry air and shelter the
cave afforded it.  There are several main passages in this diary, passage1
through passage3.
~
E
passage1~
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                           |
|   First week, Milton                                                      |
|   I've managed to find five others to help me find the crystal city the   |
|   old legends say are beyond these wastes.  I found the legends in the    |
|   ruins of a temple far away, in the middle of the wilderness.  These     |
|   others should prove helpful for a while.  When they've served their     |
|   purpose they can be discarded.  After all, there is only one treasure   |
|   worth having in the Crystal City.  And it will be *MINE*                |
|                                                                           |
|   Second week, Milton                                                     |
|   I confess I do not know exactly where the way is ... the old roads      |
|   have been swallowed up by the <blot> long ago.  But I lie to the others |
|   and they, gullible fools, believe me.  Except Tomak.  I believe he will |
|   be <blot>.  But he is easy enough to take care of.  Cyril grows more    |
|   desirable each passing hour, but she is modest in the presence of the   |
|   others.  That can be rectified easily enough.                           |
~
E
passage2~
|   Third week, <blot>                                                      |
|   I begin to wonder what Aberden writes in his notes.  The simpering      |
|   dandy was very useful in financing this venture.  But now his nasal     |
|   voice grates on mine ears.  He may be useful yet ... if only to give    |
|   to Michith when that great lout grows restless.  Gordas has been        |
|   so very useful when those damnable bugs attack ... but if he so much    |
|   as looks at me cross eyed I will tear his heart out and eat it.  I      |
|   *have* been hungry recently, after all.                                 |
|                                                                           |
|   End of Fourth Week, Milton                                              |
|   Tomak grumbled too much and was disposed of.  Gordas is apparently not  |
|   as colossally stupid as I thought.  Michith broke his neck.  Aberden,   |
|   the simp, is powerless.  Maybe it would be amusing to have Mict- <blot> |
~
E
passage3~
|   Fifth week, Milton                                                      |
|   With only Myself, aberden and michith around besides cyril, I found no  |
|   good reason behind her modesty, and so took her.  'twas entertaining.   |
|   Michith watches, which makes it <blot>.  Her screams are so beautiful.  |
|                                                                           |
|   Sixth week, Milton                                                      |
|   Michith killed Aberden last night.  Removed his head and poured his     |
|   blood on Cyril and mine entwined bodies.  Delicious!  I know the city   |
|   is somewhere near ... I can almost smell the legendary <blot>           |
|                                                                           |
|   Seventh <blot>, Milton                                                  |
|   I've found it!  A cave that *must* lead to the Crystal City!  The bitch |
|   Cyril ran away in the night, without her clothes and only a canteen.    |
|   She will not make it far.  Pity.  Michith was killed by a snake.  It    |
|   saves me the trouble of having to do it myself.  I write this just as I |
|   Am about to enter the passage to the lost Crystal City...               |
|                                                                           |
|   $^#&$@&*@$&%&$%&@#$%!@% ((@&&!#&%&!@%#$&%*@& NO!  It's a dead end! Noo  |
|   NO! NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NO NOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO...  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
~
