E
page1~
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                          |
|   A Compendium of Magical Weapons                                        |
|                                                                          |
|   This work deals with four magical weapons of this world.  There are    |
|   many others, but they are for other scholars with more knowledge (and  |
|   patience) than I to cope with.  All of them are powerful, imbued with  |
|   strange and sometimes hideous abilities.  And all four are far beyond  |
|   the reach of an ordinary mortal ...                                    |
|                                                                          |
|   ...Doombringer the Sword of Chaos is one of the most dangerous of      |
|   the four, but is by far the most mundane.  It will, on  occasion,      |
|   blur and vibrate wildly in the hands of its owner, striking the foe    |
|   not once or twice, but many, many times.  Some legends indicate that   |
|   in the hands of the truly lucky, it has struck fifteen blows to the    |
|   enemy's *ONE*.  Truly a formidable ally and frightening foe ...        |
~
E
page2~
|   ...there have been rumors in the underworld that one of Death's Angels |
|   has 'borrowed' Death's scythe ... and is wandering somewhere upon our  |
|   plane of existence.  With the scythe.  It is not known just what the   |
|   Scythe does, as Death has never had to use it on anyone.  The ones     |
|   he comes for are already dead ...                                      |
|                                                                          |
|   ...the sword of fire and flame is the third of the quartet.            |
|   Ofttimes this diabolical weapon will become engulfed in magical flames |
|   that do not harm the wielder, but shoot out to engulf a victim!  This  |
|   weapon does unkind amounts of damage when the sword strikes alone, but |
|   in combination with the fireball, most normal monsters stand not a     |
|   chance.  A handy weapon, and a must for discriminating barbecue-ers... |
~
E
page3~
|   ...perhaps the most evil of the enchanted weapons is Avernus the Life  |
|   stealer.  As the name indicates, it will, when the mood strikes it,    |
|   drain the very life force from the enemy of the wielder, dipping its   |
|   blade deep into the body and draining life.  Then, when it has drunk   |
|   deeply (I know not how damaging it is to the creature it happens to;   |
|   all that I have seen affected have died), it feeds the life energy     |
|   into the hands that hold it -- thus replenishing and healing the       |
|   sword's master...                                                      |
|                                                                          |
|   The exact locations of these enchanted weapons are not known, and it   |
|   is, I believe, all for the better.  All were, in ages past, stolen     |
|   from their human masters by the most powerful of dragons, or demons,   |
|   or monsters (the exception being the Scythe).  So these weapons are,   |
|   for better or for worse, beyond the reach of men ...                   |
|                                                                          |
|   Or so I fervently pray.                                                |
|                                                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
~
