This massive, bowl-like flower sits on the jungle floor collecting water and
adding color to the surrounding jungle.  The cool inside of the flower has
pulled water out of the humid air to collect in the bowl within.  This water
acts as an attractant to small insects and frogs that help to spread its pollen
and seeds.  The tips of the petals are white with a line of purple that extends
down to the center of the flower.
