suit of armor.  Though the outer scales are harder than the toughest metal,
the scales are quite small and fine and are connected to an extremely flexible
skin.  The craftsman that made the armor carefully trimmed away excess hide
and sealed the sides together at both the level of the skin and the scales on
the outside of the skin to insure that there are no weak points in the armor.
