chest ebonwood~
   The gold trim on this finely made chest shows an elegance that is just
short of being over-stated.  Carvings in the wood depict running deer and
jumping rabbits.  Around the gold-trimmed keyhole are two unicorns, one
facing toward the keyhole itself, the other looking out towards the
viewer.  Even without the gold, this chest would be to large to be carried
by anyone less than a giant, perhaps even two.  The chest looks sturdier
than many bank vaults in civilized cities, and was certainly stolen
somehow by the Yuan-ti.
~
