stock blood bloodstained~
&+y   This set of stocks is big enough and sturdy enough to hold even the largest&n
&+ygiant.  It is made of a hard wood that seems to have been petrified to make it&n
&+yeven stronger, and consists of three pieces.  This center piece is permanently&n
&+ymounted to the stand that is firmly planted into the ground.  Along the top of&n
&+ythe center piece, six large semi-circles have been carved out at evenly spaced&n
&+yintervals where the necks of those being punished to rest. A small semi-circle&n
&+ywhere a wrist would be placed is on each side of the large semi-circle.  Along&n
&+ythe bottom of this center piece, semi-circles have been carved which match the&n
&+yones for the wrists, only these are for the ankles.  Each section of the stock&n
&+yhas its own individual top and bottom pieces.  Each one has semi-circles which&n
&+yline up with those on the top of the center piece.  When this top piece is set&n
&+yagainst the center piece it keeps the prisoner secure by trapping his head and&n
&+yhis hands without hope of escape.  The bottom piece clamps his ankles in place&n
&+yso that he cannot even defend himself, much less escape.  Those who can see an&n
&+yaura of magic see that this stock is heavily enspelled, ensuring that whatever&n
&+ythe size of the prisoner, the stocks will shrink or grow to fit him. All along&n
&+ythe length of the stock is &+rbl&+Roo&+rd,&+y both &+Rfresh&+y and &+rdried&+y to stains, from all the&n
&+yprisoners that have been slowly carved up by the denizens of the town who like&n
&+ytheir &+mmeat&+y fresh.&n
~
