&+Weastern Tharnadian Gates.  Made of solid ivory, this statue was carved many
&+Wcenturies ago.  Small bits of grime mark the crevices that make up the
&+Wexquisite detail of the piece.  The statue is of a paladin in his mid-fifties,
&+Wwith shoulder-bobbed hair and a thick handlebar mustache.  He is depicted in
&+Whis war garb, his hands resting on the pommel of his six foot claymore.  His
&+Weyes look kind, yet fierce, and a slight smile plays across his lips.  There
&+Ware words carved in the statue's base.&n
