E
rock small~

&+g                          The Law of the Woodsman

&+g      * A ranger will protect the woods and all who reside there.
&+g      * A ranger must always fight for good, and never fall into the
&+g            dark ways of evil.
&+g      * A ranger should always help those in need, or any goodhearted
&+g            person who has less than you.
&+g      * A ranger shall know the ways of the world, travel far and wide
&+g            through distant lands, and learn them so as to be a learned
&+g            scout.
&+g      * A ranger shall always be welcome amongst creatures of the forest,
&+g           and will know the skills of woodland stealth and surprise.
&+g      * A ranger who carries extra food should always leave some in the
&+g           trees for other fellow rangers to find who may be hungry.
&+g           These secret places may be hollow trees, bushes, or small cabins.
&+g      * A ranger's greatest task is to destroy those evil beings in the
&+g           world who would seek to harm or destroy the woods and those
&+g           who live there.  This is sworn revenge of every ranger..
&+g      * And a warning; Those rangers who have fallen from the light of
&+g           goodness and purity, will be struck by the gods and lose all
&+g           of their ranger abilities, becoming a mere fighter, stripped
&+g           of honor.  Always stay within the light of goodness!


