E
water fountain daedalian onyx~
&+L   This bi-level fountain was created shortly after the construction of the
&+LGreat Spanning Bridge, as a tribute to the people who kept the city of
&+WTharnadia&+L alive.  A magnificent &+Wglass orb&+L is supported, about five feet off
&+Lthe ground, by an onyx psuedotree.  The ebon trunk splits into four leafless
&+Lbranches, each in one of the cardinal points, which hold fast the globe.  The
&+Lglass sphere has four holes drilled into its base, evenly spaced between the
&+Lflanking branches, and its top has been completely cut off.  A strong stream
&+Lof &+Bwater&+L is forced up the center of the stone pillar, through the bottom of
&+Lthe glass and into the air, where it falls back into the clear bowl of the
&+Lupper fountain.  About half the orb stays full at any given time, as the rest
&+Lpours out the perferations in its base, cascading in small waterfalls down
&+Linto the lower fountain.  Statues sit facing the four winds.  An &+Wangel&+L gazes
&+Lto the east and west, while &+wgargoyles&+L peer to the north and south.&n
~
