mithril hammer destroyer night~
&+C   This hammer seems to be made of the finest mithril. The mithril is made
&+Cin designs that show creatures that seems to made of shadows being destroyed.
&+CThe figure doing the destroying is a being bathed in golden light that is
&+Cwielding a sword of fire on them. The grip is made of solid steel, and is
&+Cwrapped in what looks to be fine leather.
&+C   This weapons story is old and is quite grand. Givin to the dwarven cleric
&+CDrogan during the Wars of Light and Shadow by the Goddess Raanna he wielded
&+Cit in the destruction of many minions of Sargon. During the last days of the
&+Cwar a small group of adventurers broke into the fortress and snuck past its
&+Cmost powerful defenders, including Maltheas, the angel of Death, and the
&+CMaster of Nightmares, and even Earlion, one of the most pwoerful mages on the
&+Cplane. They snuck into Sargon's personal area and there had a titanic battle.
&+CFinally, unable to kill them they impisoned him away in a pocket diminsion,
&+Chowever just as they finished Sargons minions and his army arrived to destroy
&+Cthem, Drogan bought the rest of the group time to flee, while he single
&+Chandedly fought off the army. The hammer has been lost since then, some say
&+Cit was destroyed, others say that it fell into the hands of the minions of
&+CSargon.                               &n
~
