corpse martin sorcerer llewellyn&n~
   This is the corpse of one of the most poweful &n&+msorcerers&n that has ever
lived. He grew up in the ancient elven city of &n&+gVel&+Gya&n&+gdin&n, on the western coast
in the time of&+W Legends&n. His mother was the&+W Silver &n&+gLady&n, the most
powerful minion of &+WCerro&n, the &+WSilver Dragon &+LGod. &nHis father was Ilvin Dealth,
another plane traveleing sorcerer. When the &n&+rwars &nof &+WLight &nand &+LShadow &ncame he
kept himself aloof from them, prefering to live in &n&+gVe&+Gly&n&+gadin&n, the city he loved.
When he came back from the planer adventure he found his beloved town laid
to waste, its people killed, and the city givin over to &n&+gdemons&n. &+WMartin &nswore
that he would see &+LSargon&n pay for that. In the next ten years he constructed
the &+LPrison &nof &+CE&+Bx&n&+bi&+Bl&+Ce&n, a pocked diminsion from which there was no escape. When
&+LSargon&n was thrust here, there was one catch. One person had to stay and seal
the prision away, and the &+Levil&n god himself, forever. &+WMartin&n decided that he
would stay here. &n&+MTime&n passes strangely here, there is no telling how long
he lived here, awayting his time to &n&+rdie&n. Some say that his &+Csoul&n lives on,
even it unable to escape the prison of his creation... who now can tell...
for that is a tale for another &+Lday&n.&+C.&+W.&n
~
