3 7000 100
E
kabuto great helmet~
This great helmet, called a kabuto, has been fashioned out of cured and
laminated leather.  It's quite a sturdy piece of work and should be enough
to protect the wearer from glancing blows to the head.  The sides of the
helmet extend to protect the ears and the back is long enough to provide
some measure of safety to the back of the neck.  It's semi-conical in
shape, coming together in a point at the top.  A band of green cloth
encircles the helmet and the symbol of the Jade Empire has been
embroidered on the band with black thread.
~
A
23 -1
