iron jingasa hat~
This hat resembles the wide, round straw hat used by peasant farmers except
for this one is made of iron instead of straw.  It doesn't have guards
for the ears, cheeks, or neck.  It would provide excellent shade from the
sun, but no real protection to those areas.  Two simple straps made of cord
extend from the side of the hat, where the ears of a wearer would be,
and they can be tied to keep it on one's head.
~
