lair gibberling king shanaanaa parchment piece paper note notes~
The Lair of the Gibberling King

Hidden at the door to the entrance is its own key. If you can, move through the 1st area invisible, it will make it much easier. Regardless you will need to move south/southeast and find the high priest G'graz. He holds a key to a secret entrance in his room. Follow through that secret to and up the Waterfall.

Once at the top of the waterfall you enter a Grotto. Head four north and two west to find the troll corpse that marks the hidden entrance towards the kings room.

There are numberous ropers and elementals that wander the grotto so you may consider clearing many of them because they can become overwelming at times. From the hidden entrance in the grotto you will need to continue down. Before you move on however you will need to know the following:

All of creatures here will chase you if you attack them in any way so its best to use this to your advantage because they are a strong horde in numbers but are weak alone.

When standing at the boulder below the grotto you must push it out of your way.
The next few rooms are packed with the Blood Horde. I like to have my conjurer send a couple elementals to block for another person who can cast a quick spell, like magic missile, onto one of the Horde members and return before getting attacked. He is instructed to die and not to flee if he does get engaged as he could flee further inside and make it difficult to move on.

Continue this pattern through the remainder of the tunnels including the room with the dracolich Crymson.

Once you have defeated Crymson you will need to return to the Entrance of the Grotto to portal if needed.

Good Luck!

P.S. Assign each of the people who have a takedown skill onto different numbers of the horde to avoid them casting spells.

P.S.S. Roshen sometimes visits the Grotto and carries a wand of dismissal. Claim it and quest it with Crymson's essence to the elemental noble south of the boulder.
~
