shanaanaa parchment piece paper note notes arachdrathos guilds drow~
Arachdrathos Guilds (Drow)

Well how you begin this can be interesting and require some understanding
on the layout of the Drow's hometown but the actual guilds are located
in the web's below the town. Once you have gained access to the webs try
and get a feel for them. They do repeat and seem endless. For example, if
you move east or west continuously you will be moving up or down layers
of the web. There are intersections in the web that allow quicker access
up and down the web and act as short cuts when moving from one house to
the other. Inside the web are drow teachers which can be a challenge to
fight but are avoidable using the intersections.

Things you need to know:
   There are five houses you need to visit, and each have two switches
   that you must activate. There is an order to the houses as well which
   I will pass onto you but so you know the switches open up rooms inside
   the other houses that hold the switches for other houses and so forth.

   Also, there are traps in place in certain objects, like chests, that
   can put everything in the room to sleep. I have not found anything
   worthwhile inside so do as you will with them.

&+CThe first house you must find is the House Olipth. These are sorcerer and
&+Cconjurers who make residance here and will fight be defend it. They have
&+Cmade a series of keys to ensure the saftey of the switches so you must
&+Copen each door with the previous key to gain the next. Find and push the
&+Ctwo switches then move on to the next house.

&+rThe second house you visit is that of warriors and the Zochra Keep. It is
&+rguarded by two golems and once you enter past the golems you can not
&+rreturn the way you came. They too have several keys, many are false, but
&+ryou need to claim the right one to move forward toward the switches at
&+rthe top of the keep. You can leave the keep one of two ways, the easiest
&+ris all down at the Adamantine Stairs. The second is past the Warmaster
&+rand his trap room south of the Landing. Just east of the warmaster is an
&+ralcove with a pool. Enter it and return to the front gates of the house.

&+mNext is the House Ilith filled with priests. The high priest holds the
&+mkey to the tower on the west side with a switch and on the east side is
&+manother switch you must push. Here with a bit of stealth and magic you
&+mcan avoid many of the inhabitants.

&+gHouse of Slin holds the masters of assassins and his followers. His chef
&+ghides the key to the masters chambers and can be found on the west side
&+gof the Commons. To the east is a forgotten room in the recreation area
&+gwhich holds the next switch. After you pressed both move to the next house.

&+WHere can be the most difficult of the houses. Necromancers call this place
&+Whome in the house of Sa'Zarn. The drows inside do not move around but will
&+Wchase you if you make them angry. This could be used to your advantage.
&+WUp into the house are the two switches your looking for as well as the
&+Wthrone room of Zargenenon the vampire.
*SPECIAL NOTE* You should avoid at all costs going all down inside this
house as it leads to the Dungeons of Abominations and mostlikely certain
death. If you get stuck in the dungeons and survive the tentamorts your
only path to freedom rests further down.

&+yAfter you have visited all five houses your final destination is the House
&+yof Zarbonesti. It has two entrances an east and west which both lead to
&+ythe same end so it matters not which one you find first. Using some form
&+yof invisibility you can avoid some of the first few guards but you eventually
&+ywill need to find the Shrine of Lolth and kill the cleric with the key to
&+ythe door to the east and the final battle. After dispatching the arch cleric
&+ythere is a narrow tunnel where a shade hides and is renown for being the
&+ypossessor of the jewel of the spider queen.

Good Luck!

P.S. The Warmaster wears the platemail of might and can be challenging to gain.

P.S.S. There is a room you can cast Gate from near the web near the backdoor.
~
