shanaanaa parchment piece paper note notes transparent tower~
The Transparent Tower

Things you need to know:
  Inside the Tower are teleporter traps that are between rooms which send
you to different places within the Tower.
  Most of the creatures inside the Tower are undead so use apprioate spells.
  There is a librarian who is looking for 3 &+mpurple tokens&n and a &+Wscepter&n and
will trade you these for a key to the Storage Closet with a lot of gear.
However, to obtain the tokens you need you have to take the scepter hidden
by Aceralde to each of the three Lords of the Tower.
  When give a Lord the scepter they return it to you hidden with a token
as well so you can put all of your inventory into a container to search for
it so that you can give it to the next Lord.

Once you enter into the Tower you have a difficult time leaving as it
begins in a Maze with Strange Lights and Prisms. But if you are brave
enough to venture inside you will want to head to the south and find
a &+bstrange blue prism&n. To move forward you need to stare into the prism.

Now you have reached the Tranlucent grid where there may be some mists
that can be waiting for you. Depending on what abilities in your group
you have you can either try to wall quickly north, south, east, and
west, or immediately after you stare into the prism move up one room.
Either way you will want to avoid moving up into the Illithid above
and clear out some of the mists on the grid, just do not enter doors.
For now!

Next there is an &+Millithid&n and a &+Gmisty fog&n who stand guard of the next
passage just above. I prefer to seperate them since they are both
agressive and will chase you. I like to do this by sending a summoned
pet into them and have a quick spell caster use magic missile upon the
misty fog and then move back down to our group. He chases and we slay.
After that I like to lure the illithid away from his room because there
is a trapped room to the east of him. This way incase my members need
to flee and memorize they can do it without going into the trap.

Collect the key from the illithid and the nice visor made of misty on
the fog and go south of the Landing of Green Mist to the door east.
Use the key and slay the mist inside the room. This comfortable room
allows people to use portal spells to gain or leave as necessary. A key
is left by the mist found here and opens a door to Aceralde's Room.

Next is dealing with aceralde and his followers. His room is up above
the Landing of Green Mist. This is another place using a summoned pet
can be of use. It is a good idea to seperate aceralde's lich and vampire
followers from him and bringing them one at a time. Each of them can
be knocked down to prevent them from casting spells so use this to your
advantage. Aceralde can also be knocked down and sometimes has some
dracolich pets so deal with these how best fits for your group but he
will track you down if you do not kill him so be careful.

Once you have defeated aceralde collect his key and unlock his desk
that is east of his Sitting Room. There is a &+Wscepter&n hidden inside and
is sought after by three seperate Lords.

&+MTaking the scepter to Lisa is the easist and is on the east path from the
&+MLanding of Green Mist. At the end of Lady Lisa's path you are teleported
&+Mback to the Pillars grid below the Landing of Green Mist.

There are two doors on the east side of this grid which both lead to more
difficult places.

&+GThe Green door is the southern most of the two and is the least difficult
&+Gof the two. Lord Gullivier resides inside and is protected by shadowy
&+Gmonsters and a blue dragon. Once you have entered the Green Door and move
&+Gwest through the teleporter trap you end up in an open field that has a
&+Ggreen pedestal at its center. This pedestal can give you an escape from
&+Ghere if needed just by crying upon it. If your strength is strong you can
&+Gdefeat the shadowy monsters and find the hidden passage to the north. Past
&+Gthe blue dragon you will find the Lord and a teleporter back to the Pillar
&+Ggrid.

&+rThe Red Door leads to a small Plane of Avernus and is loaded with devils,
&+rblobs, and pit fiends. Only the blobs can be knocked down and are very
&+rdangerous. I highly suggest having a conjurer with you who can make walls.
&+rMove through here carefully, but once you have fought your way onto the Plane
&+ryou need to find the Lord who resides just north, east, and down. He  too
&+rwants the scepter orginating from Aceralde's desk. After you have turned the
&+rscepter over to Lord Devilish head as far east as you can to a door. The
&+rdoor requires a password, ILLUSION. Open and go through it. You will need
&+rto move back east which will teleport you back onto the Pillar grid.

&+mLastly you need to visit the librarian. There is a short cut teleporter
&+mand it is found two south of the center of the Pillar grid. Make your way
&+mdown to the librarian and complete the quest by given him the 3 tokens
&+mand the scepter. To leave the librarian just move north and read the book
&+mtitled &+Y"Light and Illusion&n."

The door given by the librarian goes to the door locked north at the Landing
of Green Mist. Defeat the two mists inside and find the secret door inside.
Speak the word REALITY to unlock it, and you will gain access to the closet
full of treasure.

Good Luck!

P.S. Many of the equipment is hidden so search, and find the belt west of
of the Landing of Green Mist behind the door.
~
